        <body>
            <div xml:id="d93">

                <pb facs="0231" n="135" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg135"/>

                <head>No. 91.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Williamson to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation in Central America</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1874-01-03"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 3, 1874</date>. (Received February 5.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 90.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose you, herewith,
                    translated copies of the answers of the government of Nicaragua to my
                    communications of which I sent you copies with my Nos. 76 and 77.</p>
                <p>Your attention is respectfully called to the difference in the tone of the letter
                    of the 12th and that of the 20th. In the former no objection is raised to any
                    plan of pacification. In the latter numerous diplomatic suggestions or
                    objections are quite pointedly made.</p>
                <p>* * * * * *</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>GEO. WILLIAMSON.</signed></closer>




